%N A400938 a(n) = 1 + the total remainder when repeatedly taking integer cube roots until 1 is reached.
%C A400938 Write 1..7 in columns 1..7 of a first row. Each cube k^3 (k >= 2) starts a new row directly below k, and the following integers continue to its right until the next cube. Then a(n) is the column in which n appears.
%C A400938 a(k^3) = a(k) (immediate from the definition), so for example 2, 8, 512, 134217728, ... all lie in column 2.
%F A400938 a(n) = a(A048766(n)) + n - A048766(n)^3 for n > 1.
%F A400938 a(n^3) = a(n).
%e A400938 a(30): 30 - 27 = 3, then 3 - 1 = 2, so a(30) = 1 + 3 + 2 = 6.
%o A400938 (PARI) a(n)={my(t=0); while(n>1, my(k=sqrtnint(n,3)); t+=n-k^3; n=k); t+n}
%o A400938 (Python)
%o A400938 from sympy import integer_nthroot
%o A400938 def a(n):
%o A400938     t = 0
%o A400938     while n > 1:
%o A400938         k = integer_nthroot(n, 3)[0]
%o A400938         t += n - k**3
%o A400938         n = k
%o A400938     return t + n
%o A400938 print([a(n) for n in range(1, 76)])
%Y A400938 Cf. A336860 (square analog), A048766, A053186.
%K A400938 nonn,easy,new
